ITEMS=[]
def family(options, rows):
 assert len(options)==len(rows)==4
 for i,(q,e) in enumerate(rows):ITEMS.append((q,[options[i]]+options[:i]+options[i+1:],e))
family(['Utility','Scarcity','Desire','Effective purchasing power'],[
('A buyer values a cottage because its single-level layout meets a mobility need. Which factor of value is illustrated by that useful service?','Utility is the capacity to satisfy a need or want; it is not simply the cost of creating the feature.'),
('Only three waterfront sites are available while many qualified buyers seek that location. Which factor describes the limited supply relative to demand?','Scarcity concerns supply relative to demand, not merely a small absolute number of properties.'),
('A survey finds that households want homes with garden space, but does not establish their budgets or financing. Which factor has the survey directly established?','Desire is a wish to acquire the property. Effective purchasing power additionally requires an ability to buy.'),
('Several households want a dwelling, but only one can fund the purchase through savings and approved financing. Which factor distinguishes that household?','Effective purchasing power converts a wish into demand supported by the financial ability to purchase.')])
family(['Police power','Eminent domain','Escheat','Taxation'],[
('A municipality limits building height through a valid zoning ordinance. Which governmental power is being exercised?','Land-use and building regulations are exercises of police power for public welfare; no acquisition is described.'),
('A public authority acquires a strip of privately owned land for a road through condemnation with just compensation. Which power supports the acquisition?','Eminent domain permits acquisition for a public use with the legally required compensation.'),
('Under applicable law, ownership passes to the state after an owner dies without a will or lawful heirs. Which governmental power is involved?','Escheat provides for property to pass to the state when there is no lawful successor under the applicable rules.'),
('A county imposes an annual levy on real estate to fund public services. Which governmental power is involved?','A compulsory property levy is taxation; it is distinct from regulating use or acquiring title.')])
family(['Legally permissible','Physically possible','Financially feasible','Maximally productive'],[
('A proposed use fits the site and has a positive return, but an enforceable covenant prohibits it with no reasonable prospect of removal. Which highest-and-best-use criterion is not satisfied?','The use must satisfy relevant private as well as public restrictions. Physical fit and profit do not cure a legal prohibition.'),
('Zoning allows a house, but a documented unstable slope leaves no practicable building area. Which highest-and-best-use test is the immediate obstacle?','Physical possibility considers site conditions and whether the proposed use can actually be accommodated.'),
('A permitted, buildable project would be worth $430,000 when finished but requires $470,000 in total investment, including the site. Which highest-and-best-use criterion is not satisfied on these assumptions?','A use that cannot cover its required investment and return is not financially feasible under the stated figures.'),
('Three legally allowed, buildable and profitable uses remain. The appraiser selects the one yielding the greatest land value. Which final test is being applied?','Maximum productivity compares the value produced by the uses that survive the other tests.')])
family(['Substitution','Contribution','Anticipation','Externalities'],[
('Two available homes offer equivalent benefits without unusual delay. A purchaser refuses to pay more for one than the price of the other. Which principle explains the limit?','Substitution relates value to the cost or price of a satisfactory alternative with comparable utility.'),
('A workshop cost $38,000 to build, but verified sales indicate it adds only $16,000 to the property. Which principle makes the latter amount relevant?','Contribution measures a component by the value it adds to the whole, not automatically by construction cost.'),
('Buyers pay more today because reliable evidence indicates that a planned transit connection will improve future accessibility. Which principle directly explains their present valuation of future benefits?','Anticipation links current value with expected future benefits. Expectations still need credible market evidence.'),
('Noise from a newly operating neighboring freight terminal reduces demand for nearby houses. Which principle describes the effect of an influence beyond the parcel?','Externalities are effects originating outside the property; they can increase or decrease its value.')])
family(['Market value','Investment value','Value in use','Insurable value'],[
('An assignment seeks the price most likely under the identified open-market definition, reflecting typical purchasers rather than one named buyer. Which value concept is sought?','Market value uses the conditions in the identified market-value definition and market participants, not a single investor\'s special requirements.'),
('A buyer evaluates a duplex using that buyer\'s own tax position and required return, which differ from typical purchasers. Which value concept is being estimated?','Investment value reflects the requirements of a particular investor or class of investors.'),
('A specialist assesses the worth of a facility in its continuing use to its current operator, without assuming exchange in the open market. Which concept is emphasized?','Value in use concerns utility in a particular use and need not equal value in exchange.'),
('An assignment applies a policy\'s definition to estimate the amount associated with replacing covered improvements after a covered loss. Which value concept applies?','Insurable value depends on the insurance definition and coverage; it is not automatically the market value of land and improvements.')])
family(['A retrospective effective date','A current effective date','A prospective effective date','The report completion date'],[
('A report prepared today estimates a house\'s value on the date of a death eight months ago. How is its valuation date classified?','The effective date precedes the performance of the appraisal, so the opinion is retrospective.'),
('An appraiser estimates a property\'s value as of today using present conditions and completes the analysis today. How is its valuation date classified?','The opinion applies to current conditions on the present effective date, rather than a past or future date.'),
('An assignment estimates a project\'s value as of an anticipated completion date nine months from now. How is that valuation date classified?','A future effective date produces a prospective value opinion; assumptions must support the future scenario.'),
('An appraisal has a March 1 effective date and is signed and transmitted on March 18. Which date is March 18 in this scenario?','March 18 is the date the report was completed and communicated, distinct from the date to which the value opinion applies.')])
family(['Social forces','Economic forces','Governmental forces','Environmental forces'],[
('A rise in smaller households changes demand toward compact dwellings. Which broad influence on value best describes this demographic change?','Household composition and population patterns are social influences on housing demand.'),
('Mortgage borrowing costs increase while household demographics and land-use rules remain stable. Which broad influence is directly changing?','Interest rates and credit availability are economic influences on purchasing power and demand.'),
('A newly adopted zoning ordinance permits additional residential density. Which broad influence directly created this change?','A public land-use decision is a governmental influence, even though it may have economic effects.'),
('New flood-risk mapping identifies increased exposure from a river. Which broad influence is directly described by the physical hazard?','Flood exposure is an environmental influence; the question concerns the hazard itself rather than any resulting regulation.')])
family(['5 months','10 months','15 months','20 months'],[
('A market has 30 comparable listings and absorbs 6 per month. With no new listings and a constant pace, how long would the inventory take to sell?','Inventory divided by monthly absorption is 30 / 6 = 5 months.'),
('A project has 80 unsold units and expects to capture 40% of a market absorbing 20 units monthly. At that constant capture rate, how long will its units take to sell?','The project captures 0.40 × 20 = 8 units monthly; 80 / 8 = 10 months.'),
('An inventory initially contained 108 units. After 3 months of sales at 6 per month, with no new supply, how many more months are needed at the same pace?','Eighteen units sold, leaving 90; 90 / 6 = 15 additional months.'),
('A development sells 48 units in its first year. If that monthly pace continues, how long will its remaining 80 units take to sell?','The observed pace is 48 / 12 = 4 units monthly; 80 / 4 = 20 months.')])
family(['$12,000','$18,000','$24,000','$30,000'],[
('A $200,000 interest-only loan carries 6% annual interest with no fees. What is the interest payable over one full year?','Interest is principal × annual rate: $200,000 × 0.06 = $12,000.'),
('An annual loan payment is $28,000, of which $10,000 is interest. How much principal is repaid in that payment?','Principal repayment is total payment less interest: $28,000 - $10,000 = $18,000.'),
('A property costs $120,000 and the lender finances 80% of that price. Ignoring transaction costs, how much cash equity must the purchaser provide?','The buyer supplies the remaining 20%: $120,000 × 0.20 = $24,000.'),
('A project requires $90,000 now. Its entire future net benefit is $132,000 exactly one year later. At a 10% annual discount rate, what is its net present value?','The benefit has present value $132,000 / 1.10 = $120,000; subtracting the $90,000 initial outlay gives $30,000.')])
family(['Land','Labor','Capital','Entrepreneurship'],[
('A developer acquires an undeveloped parcel with natural resources. Which agent of production does the parcel itself represent?','Land includes the site and natural resources, distinct from work, produced assets and development coordination.'),
('Carpenters spend 900 hours framing new homes. Which agent of production is represented by their work?','Human effort directed toward production is labor.'),
('A construction firm uses manufactured cranes and concrete mixers on a project. Which agent of production do those produced assets represent?','Produced goods used in further production are capital, rather than the natural site or workers\' effort.'),
('A developer identifies unmet demand, assembles resources and accepts the risk of creating a new subdivision. Which agent of production is most directly described?','Entrepreneurship coordinates resources and bears the risks of undertaking production.')])
assert len(ITEMS)==40
